4f662ee0e063d92798f3"}, {"id": "8e221f", "text": "phenol <math><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> -ethoxyphenol <math><mo>&lt;</mo></math> methanol", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798f4"}, {"id": "8b175d", "text": "methanol <math><mo>&lt;</mo></math> phenol <math><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> -ethoxyphenol", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798f5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798f6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3a9"], "concepts": ["6162fbac6ed13040ec851b25"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements. One is labelled as Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and the other is labelled as Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>.</p><p>Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math> Annulene. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>8</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;Annulene and cis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>10</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;Annulene, are respectively aromatic, not-aromatic and aromatic.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F48e14dd2-2a22-490a-9c2b-0e42ca2bf6d0-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 266px; height: 250px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>: Planarity is one of the requirements of aromatic systems.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e622db", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are correct and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798f7"}, {"id": "8cce11", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is NOT the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798f8"}, {"id": "a9daa2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is not correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798f9"}, {"id": "e3f580", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is not correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798fa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798fb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4787"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473e"], "question": {"text": "<p>Arrange the following conformational isomers of n-butane in order of their increasing potential energy:<br /><img height=\"216\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb8cec8cd-ed86-4c2d-bcc4-e13b05ef3afa-image.png?alt=media\" width=\"800\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c263bc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>II</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798fc"}, {"id": "a4ed35", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>II</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798fd"}, {"id": "ccacb5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798fe"}, {"id": "18ba67", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92798ff"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279900", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["6162fbaf6ed13040ec851d1a"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion&nbsp;and the other is labelled as Reason.</p><p><strong>Assertion</strong>: A mixture contains benzoic acid and napthalene. The pure benzoic acid can be separated out by the use of benzene.</p><p><strong>Reason</strong>: Benzoic acid is soluble in hot water.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "383ef5", "text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279901"}, {"id": "f4c8c9", "text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279902"}, {"id": "de1164", "text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279903"}, {"id": "9a5ab4", "text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279904"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279905", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95ef"], "concepts": ["61ab7a186fe44bfe0fe4b93d"], "question": {"text": "Lassaigne's test is used for detection of:"}, "options": [{"id": "a82254", "text": "Nitrogen and Sulphur only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279906"}, {"id": "15e1ef", "text": "Nitrogen, Sulphur and Phosphorous Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279907"}, {"id": "56d584", "text": "Phosphorous and halogens only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279908"}, {"id": "e65d6d", "text": "Nitrogen, Sulphur, and halogens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279909"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927990a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8445b"], "concepts": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8441e"], "question": {"text": "Kjeldahl’s method cannot be used to estimate nitrogen for which of the following compounds?"}, "options": [{"id": "409f4b", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927990b"}, {"id": "f289cf", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi 