3d9279a0d"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d92799d9", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279945", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c53833a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87e3"], "question": {"text": "<p>Number of compounds among the following which contain sulphur as heteroatom is____.</p>Furan,Thiophene, Pyridine, Pyrrole, Cysteine, Tyrosine"}, "options": [{"id": "405d6e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279946"}, {"id": "4bcc7e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279947"}, {"id": "540efe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279948"}, {"id": "9212c8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279949"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927994a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["63299fbd17b095e01ee37427"], "question": {"text": "<p>Three organic compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;were allowed to run in thin layer chromatography using hexane and gave the following result (see figure). The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;value of the most polar compound is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F893d94dc-6b43-42df-a201-cc4011612d62.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 211px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d7261b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927994b"}, {"id": "a6773f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927994c"}, {"id": "dc81f1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927994d"}, {"id": "4e7716", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927994e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927994f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8445b"], "concepts": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8441e"], "question": {"text": "Kjeldahl&#39;s method was used for the estimation of nitrogen in an organic compound. The ammonia evolved from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of the compound neutralised <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> solution. The percentage of nitrogen in the compound is (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "68f8ed", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279950"}, {"id": "af2a01", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279951"}, {"id": "022389", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279952"}, {"id": "a37bac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279953"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279954", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927d"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f925b"], "question": {"text": "The total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> sigma bond/s in mesityl oxide <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is (Round off to the Nearest Integer)."}, "options": [{"id": "52393e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279955"}, {"id": "87db62", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279956"}, {"id": "d91f45", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279957"}, {"id": "81b251", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279958"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279959", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4787"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ef8"], "question": {"text": "The possible number of stereoisomers for 5-phenylpent-4-en-2-ol is $\\ldots\\ldots$"}, "options": [{"id": "520ec5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927995a"}, {"id": "a371fb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927995b"}, {"id": "4d1175", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927995c"}, {"id": "7d2f0c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d927995d"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:58.182Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:58.182Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f662ee0e063d9279a0e"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:04.277Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04